::code id=gate-one-system lang=sh run reads=crates,sites,Cargo.toml
# Rule 7: the deleted systems must stay deleted, and legacy words must not creep
# back into code — as a type name (struct/enum/type alias) or a constant
# (SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE), not only ever a bare `struct Foo` declaration.
#
# Two kinds of match are excluded on purpose, not by accident:
#  - Feature-level "accounts" branding that a prior round deliberately kept when it
#    renamed the per-record type Account -> ReportFiler (see docs/labs/redesign-history.dx,
#    block round-3-final-list): AccountsConfig, AccountsRuntime, and the on-disk
#    ACCOUNTS_DIR/ACCOUNTS_FILENAME names. These name the reports-accounts *feature*,
#    not the record, so they were not part of that rename and are not part of this gate.
#  - Identifiers that belong to an unrelated domain and only share a common English
#    word with the deleted RBAC system: ACME's AccountKey (RFC 8555 protocol term),
#    the three unrelated Role enums (ws framing, site Exposure config, mesh channels),
#    WebAuthn/CTAP spec flags and field limits (MAX_USER_CHARS, DEFAULT_USER,
#    FLAG_USER_PRESENT, FLAG_USER_VERIFIED), literal Win32 API names (TOKEN_USER_CLASS,
#    USER_DEFAULT_SCREEN_DPI), and the HTTP User-Agent constant.
fail=0
for p in crates/services/account-manager crates/ui/account-console scripts/deployment docs/index.dx docs/status.dx; do [ -e "$p" ] && { echo "RESURRECTED: $p"; fail=1; }; done
allowed_types='AccountsConfig|AccountsRuntime|AccountKey|^crates/net/ws/src/frame\.rs.*enum Role|^crates/foundation/config/src/lib\.rs.*enum Role|^crates/services/mesh/src/channel\.rs.*enum Role'
n=$(grep -rIn --include=*.rs -E '\b(struct|enum|type)[[:space:]]+(User|Account|Role|Permission)[A-Za-z]*\b' crates \
    | grep -vE "$allowed_types" \
    | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
allowed_consts='ACCOUNTS_DIR|ACCOUNTS_FILENAME|MAX_USER_CHARS|DEFAULT_USER|FLAG_USER_PRESENT|FLAG_USER_VERIFIED|TOKEN_USER_CLASS|USER_DEFAULT_SCREEN_DPI|USER_AGENT'
c=$(grep -rIn --include=*.rs -E '\bconst[[:space:]]+[A-Z0-9_]*(USER|ACCOUNT|ROLE|PERMISSION)[A-Z0-9_]*\b' crates \
    | grep -vE "$allowed_consts" \
    | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
echo "legacy-named types: $n"; [ "$n" -gt 0 ] && fail=1
echo "legacy-named constants: $c"; [ "$c" -gt 0 ] && fail=1
exit $fail
::end

::output id=gate-one-system-output for=gate-one-system status=ok hash=c46819532cbb385ad8d447343c790cf1d0f1c083c7bbc87cf5c289faa1653c8c
legacy-named types: 0
legacy-named constants: 0
::end

::heading level=2 id=journal
8. Journal (newest first, one line each)
::end

::bulleted-list id=journal-list
- 2026-09-19 — Outage after merging the redesign to `main`; reverted. Cause under investigation: updater stop-then-build with no restart path. Rule 8 added.
- 2026-09-19 — Decisions: no public agent door; Agents belong to a Person; Home MCP stays separate; Owner becomes a Grant.
- 2026-09-19 — dx reports filed: a2413448 (context lost between agents), 293435c9 (dx under-used by small agents), d998d78c (dx ignores .gitignore).
- 2026-09-19 — Round 1 review: 7 findings fixed (`3e0a8b6`), 3002 lib tests green on macOS.
- 2026-09-19 — Gates first run: build ok, windows check ok. `gate-test` 2974 pass / 28 fail inside dx_run — all 28 bind loopback, which the dx sandbox denies (dx report 7b16aca0); outside dx the suite is 3002/0. Until dx grants loopback, the socket tests are verified by `cargo test --lib --workspace` in a shell — the one sanctioned raw command. `gate-one-system` flags `struct Account` in `crates/services/reports/src/accounts.rs`: check against Person, rename or remove.
- 2026-09-19 — Merged `round3/owner-person`, `round3/safe-updater`, `round3/reports-account` into `redesign/round-2` (zero textual conflicts). Fixed two semantic breaks a clean merge did not surface: a stale `Accounts`→`ReportFilers` import in `crates/app/cli/src/reports_command.rs`, and a real regression in `Api::permits`'s `Demand::OwnerReads` arm that broke "reads stay open" for a demoted console password (`crates/app/admin/src/lib.rs`, caught by `crates/app/admin/tests/api.rs`). Gates green: build, 3027 lib tests, 633 admin+proxy tests, Windows check clean, `gate-one-system` legacy-named types 0. Folded `docs/architecture.dx`'s unique history into `docs/labs/redesign-history.dx` and deleted it; goals 4/5/6 left unticked — each still has a genuinely open sub-requirement (console Grant-editing UI, `init-owner`/console-password deletion, Windows CI build gate). Deleted the three merged branches locally.
- 2026-09-19 — Fixed 6 findings from a code review, each with a regression test: (1) `build_and_swap`'s rename-aside binary could be cancelled mid-build by `serve_everything`'s `tokio::select!` with no path back — closed with a `SwapGuard` whose `Drop` restores `prev` if `exe` is missing, exploiting Rust's synchronous drop of a cancelled future's locals rather than touching `main.rs`'s `select!` at all; (2) the fallback install copy was not atomic — `install_atomically` now copies to a `.installing` sibling and renames into place; (3) `restore_previous_binary`'s second rename had no fallback — `install_previous_over` now puts the discarded build back at `exe` if the restore itself fails, so a box is never left with nothing runnable (rule 8); (4) `Site.owner` validation already fixed pre-session; (5) the `round3/reports-account` rename's leftover "Account" identifiers (`AccountError`→`FilerError`, `MAX_ACCOUNTS`→`MAX_FILERS`, `MAX_FILED_PER_ACCOUNT`→`MAX_FILED_PER_FILER`, plus `ACCOUNT_ID_BYTES`→`FILER_ID_BYTES` and `MAX_PASSKEYS_PER_ACCOUNT`→`MAX_PASSKEYS_PER_FILER`, found by the widened gate below) are gone; wire-format strings (`accounts.json`, `reports-accounts/`, the `maxAccounts`/`passkeysPerAccount` JSON keys) and the deliberately-kept feature-level names (`AccountsConfig`, `AccountsRuntime`, `ACCOUNTS_DIR`, `ACCOUNTS_FILENAME`) are untouched on purpose; (6) `People::any_owner` — dead (zero non-test call sites), fully redundant with `owners()`, and its doc comment described a `selfhost init-owner` command and a `console.passwd` migration that do not exist — deleted rather than re-documented, since the sub-requirement in the gap above this line covers building that command for real. `gate-one-system` widened to catch `enum`/`const` as well as `struct` (its old blind spot, which is exactly how (5) went undetected), with a documented allow-list for the feature-level names above and for unrelated domains that share an English word with the deleted RBAC system (ACME `AccountKey`, three unrelated `Role` enums, WebAuthn/CTAP spec constants, literal Win32 API names, HTTP `User-Agent`) — re-run green: `legacy-named types: 0`, `legacy-named constants: 0`. Full suite: `cargo build --workspace` clean; `cargo test --lib --workspace` 3029/0 (matches `gate-test`'s own script, run outside dx since it binds loopback); `cargo test --workspace` (adds `selfhost-cli`'s bin-target tests, where this round's `self_update.rs` regression tests live) 4028 passed / 0 failed / 19 ignored (pre-existing hardware-dependent `home` tests plus one pre-existing ignored CLI test — none introduced this round).
- 2026-09-19 — Built `selfhost init-owner <name> --email <address>` (`crates/app/cli/src/init_owner_command.rs`): reuses `Person`/`PersonPasswords`/`Grants` rather than duplicating either; password prompted twice no-echo on a TTY (`rpassword`) or read as two stdin lines otherwise, never a CLI argument; refuses if `People::any_owner()` is already true, naming the current owners. Always writes the registry and login-password store directly, daemon running or not — the admin API's `Demand::OwnerOnly` can never be satisfied by this CLI's bearer credential (`Policy::decide` excludes `Capability::Owner` from `the_machine_may` before the owner-blanket-allow branch is reached), while both stores are read fresh on every check, so a direct write is live immediately with no restart. Re-added `People::any_owner`, deleted as dead code in the immediately preceding commit — now justified by this real caller; restored a direct assertion in `owners_reports_who_holds_the_grant`. 9 new tests, all green; gates green (build --release --locked, `cargo test --lib --workspace --locked` 99/0 shown here plus full workspace green, Windows check clean). `console-password`/`Identity::Owner` deletion still deferred to live-testing.
- 2026-09-19 — round-2 (1cbeb54) pushed to main on the owner's instruction; the box kept answering HTTPS and DNS for the first ~90 seconds watched. Open: owner runs `init-owner` on the box; then live VPN sign-in and subdomain test. Gap found: SSH needs the VPN, the VPN needs the identity system — circular, so a broken identity system locks out repair (rule 9). Next goal: break-glass relay with a pinned device key + watchdog holding the last-known-good binary.
- 2026-09-19 — TEMPORARY exception to SSH-02, owner's decision: firewall rule `TEMP-claude-ssh` allows TCP 22 from 192.168.1.31 (LAN only) for recovery, because 8444 is not answering from the LAN. MUST be removed (`Remove-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName "TEMP-claude-ssh"`) once the VPN works. Status: requested, not yet confirmed open.
- 2026-09-19 21:58 — SECOND OUTAGE: ~2 min after 1cbeb54 reached main, 80/443/53 on the box closed (host still pings; only 445 open). Cause as before: the OLD updater on the box stops the daemon, then builds. Lesson (rule 8 addendum): the first deploy of a new updater is performed by the old one — it must be done by a manual build on the box, never by a push. The TEMP-claude-ssh rule was never created (sshd likely loopback-only).
- 2026-09-19 22:15 — CORRECTION to the 21:58 entry: the old updater (f909f95) does NOT stop the daemon before building; it renames the exe aside and builds while serving. The daemon died ~2 min in, mid-build — consistent with the round-3 review finding (a sibling branch of `serve_everything`'s `tokio::select!` ends, the update future is dropped, the exe stays renamed aside, nothing can relaunch). Unproven until the box's log is read. Fixed in 1cbeb54 by `SwapGuard`; the box needs one manual build to get there.
- 2026-09-19 — Investigated a reported Windows production outage (daemon builds at HEAD but does not stay up on data/config written by old commit `f909f95`; 9191/53 accept-then-reset, 80/443 refuse, then silence). Could not reproduce on a comprehensive old-format fixture (config, sites, `console.passwd`, a Person with grants, an invite, a person-less agent) built and run with the old CLI, then started under the new daemon: it stayed healthy >90s with `selfhost health` all-serving, both before and after the fix below. Audited every `Deserialize` type on the daemon-startup path between `f909f95` and HEAD (config sections, `Site.owner`/`exposure`, agent `person: Option<PersonName>`, `service_install.rs`'s Windows Scheduled Task/keep-alive wrapper, `verify_after_restart`) — all unchanged or already tolerant of old records; no regression found. Did find and close a real gap: no fatal daemon-startup exit was ever recorded anywhere but stderr (and never even that for a panic, since the workspace builds with `panic = "abort"`, so `catch_unwind` never runs) — a Scheduled Task's wrapper output can rotate away or never attach a console at all. Added `install_startup_crash_log`/`run_daemon`/`append_startup_log` in `crates/app/cli/src/main.rs`: a `std::panic::set_hook` plus an `Err`-path write append a timestamped line to `<data_dir>/daemon-startup.log` for any startup failure, including one before `serve_everything` (e.g. a bad `--bind`), verified against the fixture to fire on an induced bad-bind and an induced port-in-use failure and to stay silent on a healthy run; 2 new regression tests. Left genuinely unresolved and stated as such: no Windows machine was available in this session (only `cargo check --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu`, which proves compilation, not linking or runtime behaviour per `HANDOFF.md`'s own caveat), so the exact reported symptom's root cause on that box remains unconfirmed.
- 2026-09-19 23:45 — ROOT CAUSE of the 21:58 outage, from the box's own log: the daemon created `pass.key` with `write_owner_only`, which refuses on Windows by design → exit at startup → wrapper loop. Fixed locally in aade225 (`selfhost_admin::pass_key`, beside `people_registry`; `peer_binding` too). Box restored by hand to f909f95 at 23:31; all sites 200. Old updater only deploys on a push nudge, so main (1cbeb54, broken on Windows) must not be nudged until the fix is on it AND rule 10 is met. Open: relay "ssh" is Down on the box even on the old build (8444 closed); data dir ACL warning (`selfhost doctor`). Earlier "SwapGuard/select!" theory for this outage: withdrawn.
- 2026-09-19 — Rule 9 (`round4/break-glass`): added `selfhost breakglass` (Ed25519 device keys, independent of People) and `selfhost watchdog` (own binary, own service registration, restarts the daemon task then restores `selfhost.prev` then rebuilds from source if needed). Job Object coupling and the relay's admin-API dependency are documented, not fixed. See `docs/labs/breakglass-watchdog.dx`.
::end
